PROJECT IMPLEMENTATION DOCUMENT: METADATA-DRIVEN AZURE DATA PLATFORM
================================================================================
Project Title: Metadata-Driven Azure Sales Data Framework & Star Schema Warehouse
Architecture: ADLS Gen2 -> ADF (Metadata Engine) -> Azure SQL Staging -> Synapse/SQL DW
Document Version: 2.0 (Complete Technical Specifications & Execution Runbook)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. ARCHITECTURAL OVERVIEW & DDL DESIGN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The database is structured into three dedicated functional schemas:
- meta: Orchestration control, data mappings, validation rules, and watermark bookmarks[cite: 1].
- stg:  Transient landing, structural quarantine, and duplicate audit logs[cite: 1].
- dw:   Presentation star schema (conformed calendar, SCD1/SCD2 dimensions, fact sales)[cite: 1].

1.1 Metadata Control Layer (meta)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE SCHEMA meta;
GO

CREATE TABLE meta.SourceSystem (
    SourceSystemId   INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY,
    SourceSystemName NVARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    Description      NVARCHAR(500) NULL,
    IsActive         BIT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
);

